## Bug Fix: Answer Marking Logic

I identified and resolved a critical bug where correct answers were being marked as incorrect in the UI.

### Root Cause
The database stores the literal text of the correct answer (e.g., `"\\( 1 \\)"`) instead of a simple option letter (e.g., `"C"`). The UI was comparing the user's selected letter against this literal value, resulting in a mismatch.

### Solution
- **[NEW] [mcq.ts](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/lib/mcq.ts)**:
    - Created a specialized utility [getCorrectLetter](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/lib/mcq.ts#36-64) that finds the correct option label (A, B, C...) by matching the literal answer string against the current question's options array.
- **[MODIFY] Components & Hook**:
    - Integrated this utility into `TakeMcqPracticeView`, [QuestionCard](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/modules/services/ui/components/question-card.tsx#38-307), and [PracticeResultView](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/modules/services/ui/views/practice-result-view.tsx#35-175).
    - Now, all internal checks (audio feedback, status indicators, and final review) use the correctly mapped letter.

